# .egress-allow — third-party network hosts this repo is ALLOWED to contact.
# Committed, so every clone agrees on what egress is intentional. One hostname
# per line; a host also covers its dot-boundary subdomains. See
# privacy-guard/templates/egress-allow.example for the full contract.
#
# This server is otherwise self-contained: the library, its covers, its notes
# and its OPDS feed are all served from this origin. The one external service
# below is opt-in at runtime — Settings → Privacy gates every call to it, and
# an install that never turns it on makes no outbound request at all.

# Open Library (Internet Archive) — book metadata lookup for the import
# enricher and the sorting bench's shelf sweep, plus cover images under
# covers.openlibrary.org, which this entry also covers.
#
# Anonymous, at the one-request-per-second rate their policy publishes for
# anonymous callers (https://openlibrary.org/developers/api). The faster
# identified tier is deliberately declined: it is bought with an operator's
# contact address, which is theirs to give rather than this code's to send.
openlibrary.org

# Not listed on purpose, because they are not egress: opds-spec.org, purl.org
# and w3.org appear only as XML namespace identifiers in the OPDS feed,
# idpf.org only as the OPF package namespace in the EPUB test fixtures, and
# specs.opds.io and docs.ankiweb.net only as reference links inside comments.
# None of them is ever fetched.
